Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-08-2001||05:28 PM|||| Just ordered a set of KMC 782's 17x7 +40 5x100. I need a tire size to go with it. My 85GT is lowered, and I am dead set on Yokohama A520's. But what size? The 235/ZR40's sound to tall? What should I look for? TIA <P>Peace, B2 OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 04-08-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000001||sjp777||04-08-2001||06:32 PM||||215/45/17 on the front, 235/40/17 on the rear seems to work nicely with lowering springs||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||04-08-2001||10:26 PM||||  Triple-7, I liked your website. That's one nice car you have. I'm thinking my next on will be a fast back. I'll probably stay with  the 86 or 87 because of parts avilability and cost. But I remember things and those taillights are one of them. If I get a fast back, I will be looking for a N* with an auto. Thanks for the info!<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||12
Z||000003||Thecrewchief1||04-09-2001||12:44 AM||||245-40/17's are the same height (24.7") as the factory 205-60/15. Just a thought.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||04-09-2001||07:24 AM||||   Very well, that's goodto know. Only problem, the 85GT came stock with 14's. How does that compute? LMK.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||7
Z||000005||Greg Piet||04-09-2001||09:27 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html</A> <BR>is a tire size calculator<P>stock 14" are 215/60 which is comparable to the 205/60/15<P>If you want stock overall size for a certain attribute, just use the calculator above as it tells you all the info I think you want.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72 Race Director<BR>#47 CSP<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">   <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||1
